  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 845781,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "*0-kyū Shōgi: Shōgi Yōchien Ayumi-gumi* (0から始める将棋 奨励会育成会 鮎美組) is a charming and accessible introduction to the traditional Japanese board game of Shogi (Japanese chess) for the Sony PlayStation. Designed for beginners, the game features a friendly and encouraging tutorial led by the titular \"Ayumi-gumi\" – a group of young shogi students. \n\nPlayers learn the rules and strategies of Shogi through a series of lessons and practice matches, gradually progressing from the basics to more complex maneuvers. The game offers a variety of difficulty levels, ensuring that players of all skill levels can enjoy the experience.  Beyond the tutorial, players can challenge the computer in standard matches or test their skills against friends in two-player mode.  With its cute character designs, clear explanations, and gradual learning curve, *0-kyū Shōgi: Shōgi Yōchien Ayumi-gumi* is a perfect way to discover the elegance and challenge of Shogi."
    },
